@title Manual TLS Certificate Rotation
@subtitle Public load balancer certificates
@author Edge team, Sycamore Travel

## Certificates

data certs = Domain,Expires,Days left; www.sycamoretravel.example,2026-11-14,29; api.sycamoretravel.example,2026-11-02,17; partners.sycamoretravel.example,2027-01-20,96; status.sycamoretravel.example,2026-10-30,14
table certs sort=Days left

!! **Most urgent:** status.sycamoretravel.example expires on 2026-10-30, in 14 days.

## Steps

1. Request the new certificate in the certificate manager.
2. Validate it via the DNS record.
3. Wait for the status **Issued**.

!! Never remove the old certificate first. Clients will get handshake errors until the new one is attached.

4. Attach the new certificate to the listener on `edge-alb-prod`.
5. Test with an external checker.
6. Remove the old certificate after 24 hours.

! This is manual for now because the automated renewal job is broken until ticket EDGE-812 is fixed.
